  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1999-p14.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(H\\) be where the altitude from \\(B\\) to \\(\\overline{AD}\\) intersects \\(\\overline{AD}.\\)\n\nThen we have that \\[ AH = \\dfrac{16 - 8}{2} = 4, \\] since \\(AB = CD.\\)\n\nWe then have that \\[ AB = \\sqrt{4^2 + 3^2} = \\sqrt{25} = 5. \\]\n\nThen the perimeter is \\[ 8 + 16 + 2 \\cdot 5 = 34. \\]\n\nThus, D is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Drop an altitude from \\(B\\)",
        "The two side right triangles have horizontal leg \\(4\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
